* CABSRT02 - SORT EDITED USAGE AHEAD OF OCN/BAN VALIDATION
* SORTS TELCABS.CABS.USAGE.EDITED INTO OCN/BAN/SEQ ORDER SO
* CABING02 CAN CACHE OCN LOOKUPS ACROSS A CONTIGUOUS RUN OF
* THE SAME OCN (SEE THE V1.30 1998 NOTE IN CABING02 - THE
* CACHE ONLY HELPS IF THE INPUT ARRIVES IN THIS ORDER).
*
* THE OMIT COND DROPS FATAL EDIT-STATUS RECORDS (STATUS 6-9)
* BEFORE THEY EVER REACH CABING02.  THAT IS PER CABS-STD-033 - A
* FATAL RECORD HAS ALREADY BEEN DIVERTED TO SUSPENSE BY
* CABING01 AND SHOULD NOT BE VALIDATED A SECOND TIME.  IF
* THIS OMIT IS EVER REMOVED, CABING02 WILL DOUBLE-SUSPEND
* THE SAME RECORDS AND THE CONTROL TOTALS WILL NOT BALANCE.
 SORT FIELDS=(5,4,CH,A,9,13,CH,A,22,9,CH,A)
 OMIT COND=(30,1,CH,GE,C'6',AND,30,1,CH,LE,C'9')
 OPTION EQUALS
 RECORD TYPE=F,LENGTH=200
